  "fixtureStopped": true,
  "conclusions": [
    "Foreground color-mix resolves against the corresponding parent highlight color, which is black when no ancestor supplies one. A blue parent highlight yields a blue/white mix.",
    "Direct currentColor can use the lower painted layer. Background and decoration color-mix use originating/computed highlight color instead; in these cases red/white while the glyphs paint blue.",
    "Shadow color-mix in the observed cases uses the painted highlight foreground; the shadow is blue/white even where CSSOM reports red/white.",
    "These observations invalidate the current draft treatment of all color expressions as late-resolved against lower layers. Further implementation changes are required."
  ]
}
